16.03.2023
*bouble*
Reut: It is kind of chilly, here, at the entrance for my apartment's building. I sure hope the delivery guy will come pick up my broken laptop for the repair lab quickly!
Delivery Guy: Dobrý den, nemohu to vyzvednout. Notebook je potřeba zabalit do speciálního obalu.
Reut: Sorry, I don't speak Czech -- let me open Google Translate. 
Delivery Guy: ŽÁDNÝ! TO NEMŮŽU VYZVEDNOUT! NEZABALIL JSTE TO SPRÁVNĚ
Reut: Why are you screaming at me? I don't understand what you're saying!

Passer-by: Hey, is everything okay? Let me help. He is saying that you need to pack it differently. He will come back later.
Reut: Oh... sorry, I didn't know. Thanks for the help. 
Reut: Wait, Professor Pacovský, is that you? What are the chances? 
Prof. Pacovský: Yes, it is me. What a surprise! How are you?
Reut: Forgetting the emberesment of a professor seeing me in my pijamas, I'm okay. I'm quite stressed, I've been looking for an advisor for my individual software. I've been exploring many options, but none seem suitable. There's only one month until the selectin deadline. 
Prof. Pacovský: What is the project about?
Reut: I'm not entirely sure yet. I love music and video games, so I am thinking about something related to those.
Prof. Pacovský: Oh, well, we can work togther on the ISP, but I won't be available as an advisor for the bachelor's thesis. Since you mentioned the project is about music, and you want it to continue for a thesis, Mgr. Jan Hajič, Ph.D. (bold) comes to mind. 
Reut: Oh, I haven't seen him during my search. I will check the option out. Thank you for the suggestion, and the free translation services!
Prof. Pacovský: No worries. I will see you in C# practicals next 
Reut: Bye until then. 


